Add a synchronous, cross-process memory ledger to vcann-rt.

The pinned upstream implementation checks DCMI process memory before each allocation.
That observation is asynchronous, so rapid allocations can all see stale usage and
collectively exceed the configured quota. This patch pre-charges allocations under a
process mutex and cross-process flock, records pointer/size ownership, refunds successful
frees and failed real allocations, and reclaims slots left by dead processes. The same
ledger backs rtMemGetInfoEx and enpu-monitor.

Apply to ubs-virt bac3d461c9312acfaa388bed89e9ed2a61971d1a, subdirectory
ubs-virt-enpu/vcann-rt. Apply before 0003-dsmi-use-synchronous-ledger.patch.

